# Only the trusted runner operator receives these fixed native operations.
# Path arguments are data: the helper rejects non-absolute/root/symlink trees.
# Seal/unseal accept exactly a job UUID and a state root; the seal plan is stdin.
# Their state/workspace authority is restricted by /etc/motor-runner/source-seal.json.
# Check-staging-links/remove-staging accept a repository key, fill UUID and state
# root, restricted by the same authority to build-bases/KEY/staging-UUID only.
# Each form ends in one trailing wildcard: sudo-rs, Ubuntu's default sudo since
# 25.10, accepts a wildcard only as the last argument. The helper itself refuses
# any argument count other than its fixed one.
@OPERATOR@ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/libexec/motor-runner-permissions physical-chmod owner-rwX -- *, /usr/local/libexec/motor-runner-permissions physical-chmod private-rwX -- *, /usr/local/libexec/motor-runner-permissions seal *, /usr/local/libexec/motor-runner-permissions unseal *, /usr/local/libexec/motor-runner-permissions check-staging-links *, /usr/local/libexec/motor-runner-permissions remove-staging *
